Date:     Sat, 18 Dec 93 11:51:07 EST
From: cards@top.cis.syr.edu
Subject:  Personal opinions on shotguns and handgun caliber

I am personally quite familiar with revolvers, semiautomatic pistols,
bolt action rifles, lever action rifles, selective fire (switch
chooses semiauto or full auto) rifles and shotguns.  for home defense,
I definitely recommend shotguns.  Why?

1) Nobody is seriously trying to ban them just yet.

2) ANYBODY can hit their target at close range,
even without training, even in a panic.

3) Widely available guns and ammo at reasonable prices
without registration in most states.

For personal defense, I recommend revolvers, for reliability.
Semiautomatic weapons jam, revolvers don't.

Regarding caliber... The FBI tested a variety of handguns
a while back, to select a standard weapon for their agents.
I use their data (as reported in the _American Rifleman_
magazine of the NRA) but not their choice.  The only
handgun for which ammo is widely available that will
kill a man reliably after passing through automotive
window glass is the .44 magnum.  Sometimes, a .41 mag,
.357 mag or 10mm will do it, but not consistently.
Why would I want to shoot somebody through a closed
car window? I dunno, it just makes me feel more secure
to know that I could if I had to.

If you are not a well-trained shooter but you want
to be able to defend yourself, definitely get a
shotgun.  It makes it easy to hit your target,
but unlikely that you will accidentally shoot
a friendly (since the barrel length makes it obvious
where it is pointed, unlike a handgun which can be
waved around a lot with little awareness of where
it is pointing).

just my opinions... those of a country boy...
